+# smallpt playground
+
+Kevin Beason's open-source C++ smallpt path tracer compiled to WebAssembly, with a static browser interface. Rendering runs entirely on the device inside a Web Worker. No backend or runtime package dependencies are needed.
+
+Open `index.html` through any static web host (workers and WASM need HTTP/HTTPS). The initial scene renders automatically. Randomize colors generates new wall and sphere reflectances and starts a fresh render; quality, reset, fullscreen, and PNG download controls are available. The included preview is also rendered by the compiled WASM module.
+
+## Build
+
+Install Emscripten and put `emcc` on your PATH, then run:
+
+```sh
+npm run build
+```
+
+This regenerates the committed `smallpt.js` and `smallpt.wasm`. Deploy the root static files together, including `worker.js`, `preview.png`, and `src/` for source/license links. Serve `.wasm` as `application/wasm` for streaming compilation; Emscripten can fall back to ArrayBuffer instantiation.
+
+## Source and license
+
+Original: https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/ by Kevin Beason, 2008.
+
+`src/smallpt-original.cpp` is the unmodified upstream source. `src/smallpt.cpp` preserves the intersection and radiance core and replaces the command-line PPM writer with an exported progressive RGBA renderer and color setters. Four subpixels per pixel accumulate samples independently, retaining the original tent filter, gamma conversion, and material models. OpenMP is omitted; the browser uses a dedicated worker without cross-origin isolation requirements. `src/LICENSE.txt` contains the upstream MIT license.
